"""IB DP Global Politics (SL/HL, first assessment 2026), year 2 – ib-g12-political-science.

Content pack for the QB-IB engine. Year 2 covers the thematic study Peace and Conflict (contested meanings
of peace, conflict and violence; causes and types of conflict; conflict dynamics and third-party
intervention; post-conflict transformation), the HL global political challenges (borders, security,
environment, poverty, health, identity, technology, equality), and the engagement project / HL Paper 3.

Items use the Global Politics key concepts (power, sovereignty, legitimacy, interdependence, rights, justice,
liberty, equality, development, sustainability, peace, conflict, violence), named theorists (Galtung,
Collier, Kaldor, Zartman, Lederach, Paris, Sen, Buzan) and real, dated case studies. Source extracts are
attributed to real authors, organisations and documents and are paraphrased or adapted.

Item styles
  * C1 – define / identify / state (short and MCQ),
  * C2 – explain / distinguish / correct a misconception,
  * C3 – case-based explanation and Paper 1-style source items (identify; explain with reference to a source),
  * C4 – evaluate / discuss / to what extent, Paper 2 essays (15 marks, markbands).

Mock = one HL paper set mirroring examPattern in targets.json (paper marks UNVERIFIED there); 11 items, 113 marks:
  Paper 1 (1 h 15, source-based, Peace and Conflict): Q1 identify 3 + Q2 explain 4 + Q3 compare 8 + Q4 evaluate 10,
  Paper 2 (1 h 30): four essay prompts on the thematic study, candidates answer two (15 marks each),
  Paper 3 HL (1 h 30): three stimulus-based questions on a global political challenge (4 + 9 + 15).
"""
